-- title:
--   The joint law Q of the testing construction (J, Z)
-- statement:
--   This predicate characterizes the **joint testing measure** $Q$ of Wainwright's
--   construction, p. 487: the law of the pair $(J,Z)$ generated by (1) sampling $J$ uniformly
--   from $[M]$, then (2) sampling $Z \sim P_{\theta_j}$ given $J=j$.
--
--   For a distribution family `measure : Idx → Measure 𝒳`, representatives `Prep : Fin M →
--   Idx`, and a candidate joint law $Q$ on $[M]\times\mathcal X$,
--
--   $$
--   Q \text{ is the joint testing measure} \;:\Longleftrightarrow\; \forall j\in[M],\ \forall
--   s \subseteq \mathcal X \text{ measurable},\quad Q(\{j\}\times s) = \tfrac1M\,
--   P_{\theta_j}(s).
--   $$
--
--   Setting $s = \mathcal X$ recovers "$J$ is uniform over $[M]$"; the full family of
--   equations recovers "$Z$ conditional on $J=j$ has law $P_{\theta_j}$".
--
--   **Formalization Note** $Q$ is realized directly on the product space $[M]\times\mathcal X$
--   (with $J := \mathrm{fst}$, $Z := \mathrm{snd}$) rather than via an abstract probability
--   space with separate random variables $J,Z$ mapping into it — the canonical, coordinate
--   realization of any pair with the stated joint law, and mathematically equivalent to the
--   book's more general phrasing. This sidesteps needing Mathlib's general conditional-measure
--   (disintegration) machinery: the single family of slice equations above is exactly
--   equivalent to "$J$ uniform, $Z\mid J=j \sim P_{\theta_j}$" without invoking it.
-- source:
--   Wainwright, High-Dimensional Statistics, CUP 2019, p. 487 (PDF p. 507)

import Mathlib

open MeasureTheory

namespace HighDimStat.Minimax

/-- `Q` is the **joint testing measure** of Wainwright, *High-Dimensional Statistics* (2019),
p. 487: the law of the pair `(J,Z)` generated by (1) sampling `J` uniformly from `[M]`, then
(2) sampling `Z ∼ P_{θⱼ}` given `J=j`. Realized directly on the product space `Fin M × 𝒳`
(`J := Prod.fst`, `Z := Prod.snd`), with the defining property stated as the measure of every
"slice" `{j} × s`: `Q({j} × s) = (1/M) · P_{θⱼ}(s)`, which simultaneously encodes both "`J` is
uniform over `[M]`" (take `s = univ`) and "`Z` conditional on `J=j` has law `P_{θⱼ}`". -/
def IsJointTestingMeasure {𝒳 Idx : Type*} [MeasurableSpace 𝒳] {M : ℕ}
    (measure : Idx → Measure 𝒳) (Prep : Fin M → Idx) (Q : Measure (Fin M × 𝒳)) : Prop :=
  ∀ j : Fin M, ∀ s : Set 𝒳, MeasurableSet s →
    Q ({j} ×ˢ s) = (1 / (M : ENNReal)) * measure (Prep j) s

end HighDimStat.Minimax


